00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.420
Farewell Party for Uramichi Oniisan

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:31.680
When I look back, the time
I spent as a gymnast Oniisan

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.800
seems both long and short
at the same time.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.640
Uramichi-<i>san</i>...

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:43.360
Those days I spent with you
are very precious to me.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.440
All my weight training
helped me in this workplace.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.690
I think this job was my calling.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:50.860
--Uramichi Oniisan!
--I wanna touch it!

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.660
There's a watermelon on your arm!

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.370
A new era has dawned!

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.280
It's a runaway bus!

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.070
What?

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.830
Nice bulk!

00:00:57.830 --> 00:00:58.490
What?

00:00:57.830 --> 00:00:59.960
It's standing out!

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.460
Pull-apart ab bread!

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.040
Usahara... What're you doing?
Shout like the others.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:05.670
What?

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.840
Just shout, Usahara!

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.010
What? I don't want to.

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.970
Usahara...

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.510
Usahara...

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:14.760
Stop it.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.310
Stop it!

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.640
Hey, are you still asleep?

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:28.320
Yeah... I was dreaming.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.990
I think it's a prophetic dream.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.030
Script

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.540
It was a dream about
Uramichi-<i>san</i>'s farewell party.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:44.170
I wonder if this is a revelation from God
telling me to be its organizer.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.220
What?!

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:53.760
I was mistaken?!

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:55.890
What?

00:01:55.890 --> 00:02:00.020
The gym he's been going to
is moving, so he's quitting it?

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.810
Yeah.

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:04.020
Oh...

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.020
Hm?

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.900
Did you know about it?

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.110
Yeah.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:10.400
Why didn't you tell me?!

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.860
Because you didn't ask.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.030
What kind of answer is that?

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.410
If you knew, you should've told me!

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:24.000
Like I said, you didn't ask, so...

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.670
Jeez...

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.630
Ah! Uramichi-<i>san</i>!

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:31.550
That wasn't nice!

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:32.710
What're you talking about?

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:38.510
I'm saying, why didn't you
tell me the truth?!

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:39.720
Huh?

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:43.140
Well, I have no idea
what you're talking about.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.680
Ah! Wait...

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:50.980
Ah... Yeah, yeah, yeah. It was just
me making a big fuss for nothing.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.200
Cheer up.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:04.450
Episode 13:        Together with Maman Forever

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.790
How long is this segment gonna go on for?

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:23.010
What? What the...

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.930
U-Uramichi-<i>kun</i>.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:25.930
What?

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.980
P-Please...

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:33.020
Help me.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.240
I can't...

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.820
I can't come up with any ideas!

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.450
Amon-<i>san</i>?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:44.240
Previous hit ideas 'Long, Hot Summer'
"Character that surpasses these

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:47.410
Th-The idea you suggested,
Yakumi Shinobi, was a big hit, right?

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.130
Well, about that...
I just said something random.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:53.500
I want to create something
that surpasses it!

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:57.590
I want it to surpass these

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.970
But I can't surpass my old work alone!

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:00.340
I need your help!

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.890
Well, look carefully.

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.640
The quality of it... It's not great.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:07.850
"Big hit ideas"

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:13.360
Now that we've put such great work like
"Yakumi Shinobi" out into the world,

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:16.480
nothing less than is allowed.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.780
When it's like this?

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.370
So please...

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.530
Help me!

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:24.620
Hm?

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.750
I-I can't.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:33.750
Why?! You don't even care
if my reputation gets damaged?!

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.300
I don't really... care!

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:42.140
Uramichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:43.390
Wait!

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:46.850
Your life and mine depend on it!

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:48.430
Uramichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.600
Please don't abandon me!

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.810
Uramichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:53.810
Hm?

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:58.030
Kumatani. Let's go home
before he drags us into--

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:10.710
He ran away so quickly...

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:11.870
Hm?

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.830
Hey! You guys over there!

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.050
Did you see Uramichi-<i>kun</i>?!

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:22.300
H-He went that way.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.810
He did?! Thanks!

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:31.940
Uramichi-<i>kun</i>! Uramichi-<i>kun</i>! Uramichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.600
He's so dumb.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.480
It's a good thing that
he's dumber than I thought.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.440
So, he really is dumb, huh?

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.900
Anyway, what on earth
did you do, Uramichi-<i>san</i>?

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.410
I definitely didn't do anything!
Definitely not!

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.160
He's stressing it too much.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:51.120
Oh, more importantly, Uramichi-<i>san</i>...
dinner. Let's go out for dinner. Dinner.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.660
I'm broke this month.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.250
When are you not broke?

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:56.920
I hid you from the guy, didn't I?

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.330
"Mud Boat"
"Izakaya"
"Beer"

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:07.850
Ahh... I wanna be funny...

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:09.600
What's the matter?

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:13.060
Well... I feel like someone
has been watching me.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.770
Watching you?

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.650
I guess I'm imagining things.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.570
Uramichi-<i>san</i>. Let's go
out for drinks again.

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:21.900
Good night.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.700
Yeah, good night. Be careful going home.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:25.820
Okay!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:27.490
Hey, walk straight.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.370
I <i>am </i>walking straight.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:30.660
Do you wanna stop by another place?

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.330
No, I don't.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.120
Thank you very much!

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.550
I'm sorry, Uramichi-<i>kun</i>.

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:44.420
I didn't wanna do something like this,

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.550
but I just want to create a good
work no matter what it takes

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:50.390
in order to bring surprises
and smiles to children.

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:53.640
So, I'll be watching you for a while.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:02.280
Enters a convenience store.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:03.990
Can't decide on beer.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:06.070
We're running a promotion right now.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:09.370
If you spend more than 700 yen,
you can draw from the lottery once.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:09.370
More than 700 yen...

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.320
Instant Lottery

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.790
Oh, congratulations!

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.860
"Special Prize:
Extra-large baguette cushion"

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.870
Here's the special prize.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.580
No, thanks. I don't want it.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:14.910
Whoa!

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.960
Thank you very much!

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:24.210
"Greet with all your might"
"Hello Squad"

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.710
Hello Squad!

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:28.180
Kids who can say hello energetically...!
Gather around!

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.850
The Hello Squad is here!

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:37.810
Both pandas and humans
look better with a long shot.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.980
I'm Miss Ni Hao.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:41.640
Miss Ni Hao 

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:46.990
How you dodge a bull charging at your
unguarded heart is the secret of life.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:48.530
I'm Mister Hola!

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.570
Mister Hola

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:54.830
I want to be someone as great
as the Grand Canyon, hop!

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:56.580
I'm Hello Rabbit, hop!

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.370
Hello Rabbit

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:03.340
I want to commend the person
who started the trend

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.460
of putting boiled eggs
in curry soup, <i>kuma</i>!

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:07.630
I'm Namaste Bear!

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.300
Namaste Bear

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:13.140
I'm a god born from the grudge
of a baguette that became stale

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:16.270
because it didn't come
with a storage bag for it.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:18.310
The name is Bonjour Man.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.140
Bonjour Man

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:30.360
How come... you're the only one
who's always dressed like that?

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.160
I, Bonjour Man, want to know
the answer to that more than anyone!

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:35.830
If I find out, I'm sure
I can die in peace.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:39.250
Now, let's sing the hello song together!

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:42.460
Who can say hello energetically?

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:46.090
Let's say "hello" loud--

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:48.630
I... I'm sorry.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:52.760
Bonjour.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.720
P-Please don't make eye contact with me!

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.560
This is terrible.

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:00.640
This is... exactly what I wanted.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:03.900
This is indeed my magnum opus!

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:06.020
Bravo!

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:12.450
The "Hello Squad" became even more
popular than "Yakumi Shinobi."

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:16.160
And the baguette cushion
became a punching bag.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:22.120
Uramichi Oniisan.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:25.840
That's terrible!

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:28.760
I'm so worried.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:31.130
I don't know what to do.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.390
Should I report it to the police?!

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:36.600
No. He shouldn't have gone too far.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:40.060
First, we'll do everything
we can to find them!

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:41.690
Thank you!

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.180
{=4}m 539 172 l 827 172 827 328 539 328

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.180
{=3}Green Room for
Uramichi Omota-sama

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:52.200
It'll finally be the last episode.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:53.360
What will?

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.910
What? A drama that's popular right now.
Haven't you been watching it?

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.080
Nope.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:02.080
Man, I'll miss it after it's over, but I'm
looking forward to the final episode.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.830
I wonder what's going to happen.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:06.380
That's a slice-of-life drama, right?

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.670
Even though it's the final episode,
I doubt anything unusual will happen.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.970
Jeez... You don't get it, do you?

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:17.100
No matter what show it is, something big
always happens in the final episode.

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:22.980
For example... Let's see... A child
who came to see the show gets lost.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:26.560
We'd probably look for them
until we get exhausted, right?

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:30.900
Then, we'd find them in a park that's
glowing nicely from the setting sun!

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:35.450
And the highlight, the final scene where
the mother and child get reunited!

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.580
Isn't that moving?!

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.580
"Cast"

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:42.330
<i>Together with Maman</i>:
Lost Children... Just kidding.

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:43.960
It's too corny.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:45.750
Don't underestimate the audience.

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:47.420
So harsh...

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:49.830
Hm?

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.340
Guys! There's a problem!

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:54.760
One of the kids who're going
to be on the show is missing!

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:56.510
What?!

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:59.800
It'll be fine. I'm sure he's close by.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.430
Yeah... But...

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.680
Utano Oneesan!

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.520
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.650
There's a problem!
A boy seems to be missing.

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:12.860
When I took my eyes off of him
just for a second, he...

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:14.650
What do I do?!

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:17.320
Ma'am, please calm down.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:21.370
Let's split up and check
the places children like to--

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:22.620
Hm?

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:25.330
Hm?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.250
What're you guys all doing here?

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.210
He's right here.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:29.790
Hm?

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:33.840
Seriously...! I told you
not to wander off!

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:36.220
I'm sorry!

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:40.100
I'm sorry for all the fuss.
See you later, then!

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:41.810
See you later!

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:47.560
W-Well, it's wonderful
that we found the boy.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:51.060
It is, though I can't deny the
anticlimactic feeling that I'm having.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:55.610
Seriously, what an
alarmist mother and child.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.700
By the way, where's Iketeru Oniisan?

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:02.120
Ah... He said he had to discuss
something with the stagehands

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.660
and headed to the studio.

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:09.710
Discussing something?
Do we have to be there?

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:12.380
Derekida-<i>san </i>said it wasn't necessary.

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:15.130
Don't worry. It's too much
of a hassle, anyway.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:15.710
Hm?

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:18.680
Oh? It's Derekida-<i>san</i>.

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:20.430
I wonder what he wants.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:23.510
Hello? Is something the matter?

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:23.510
He might want us there or something.

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:25.060
What?!

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:28.560
This is terrible! He said that
Iketeru Oniisan got injured!

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:29.520
What?!

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:30.980
He's bleeding!

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:34.320
Doesn't this seem like something
that would happen in the final episode?

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.360
This is no time for that!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.360
Let's go!

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:41.490
Where's Iketeru Oniisan?!

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.410
Over there!

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:45.580
Iketeru Oniisan!

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:46.910
Hm?

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.620
What's the matter?
Why are you all so flustered?

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:55.500
It seems that his hangnail
got caught on something!

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.760
Use some merbromin on it. It'll heal soon.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:59.880
"Merbromin"

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:00.090
"My boner"...

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:02.220
Iketeru-<i>kun</i>. Do you know
what merbromin is?

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:07.100
It kind of sounds like... "my boner."
I thought you said "my boner"...

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.640
Well, it's good that
it wasn't a bad injury.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:11.900
The show could get canceled
if it was really bad.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:11.900
It definitely sounds like it.

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:13.060
"My boner"... That's just...

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:13.890
Shut up.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:15.070
Ah, right. I'm sorry.

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:19.490
At any rate, on the way here,
I was really afraid

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:23.450
that we might arrive to
a bloody and gruesome scene.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.120
"Bride and groom"?!

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:30.160
What? Well, um... I said "bloody and
gruesome." You know, "blood."

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.460
Come to think of it,
is the shoot starting soon?

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:35.340
No... We'll just have to wait
and bide our time.

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.460
"Bride"?!

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.550
Oh, no... Neesan has...

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.300
Bride and groom. Bride...
Marriage, marriage, marriage...

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:44.010
...finally gone crazy...!

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.100
Marriage, marriage...

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:50.770
Oh? Is that your boyfriend?

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:52.980
Hello? What's up?

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:54.560
Uh-huh... Uh-huh...

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.770
What?! G-Getting married?!

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.110
No way!

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.700
Getting married...

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.080
Getting married...

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.830
Getting married!

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.630
A marriage proposal? Now?

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:19.130
Ending with a marriage is one of the
typical events in a final episode, right?

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:22.010
I'm happy for you, Neesan.

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:22.540
What?

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:23.300
Hm?

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:25.010
No?

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:29.470
What? Your <i>senpai </i>is getting
married? So you want me

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:33.230
to lend you money for a gift for him?

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:34.940
It wasn't the case at all.

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:37.520
Let's run before she
vents her anger on us.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.110
Something horrible will happen.

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:42.400
What? What did you say?
I wasn't listening.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.610
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:48.870
Um... Don't we have to ask
Utano Oneesan to come with us?

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:51.830
We don't have to right now.
Let's leave her alone.

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:55.120
Seriously, her boyfriend is fearless.

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.670
Look who's talking.

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:58.080
What're you talking about?

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:00.840
Iketeru!

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:01.710
Hm?

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:05.090
Sis! What're you doing here?

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:06.510
Iketeru...

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:10.350
Sayuri-<i>san</i>...

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.600
What happened?

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:19.480
Wh-What happened to Sayuri-<i>san</i>?

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:24.860
Sayuri-<i>san </i>won the Very Good Girl Award
in a dog park competition!

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:26.900
"Very Good Girl Award"
"Dog Park Competition 20th place"
"Sayuri-<i>chan</i>"

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.530
Th-That's incredible!

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:33.410
You're amazing, Sayuri-<i>san</i>!

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:36.330
That's because Sayuri-<i>san</i>
is a very good girl, right, Sis?!

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:40.540
Yeah! She's such a good girl!

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:43.050
Okay, then! Let's snuggle with her, Sis!

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:45.260
Yeah! Let's snuggle!

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:49.300
"Very Good Girl Award"
"Marriage Registration"
"Merbromin" "Notice of discontinuation"

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:49.260
Uramichi Oniisan.

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:53.850
No final-episode-esque event is happening.

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:57.440
Now that it's come to this,
let's make it happen with our own hands!

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.690
He's starting to say weird stuff.

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:00.690
Hm?

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.860
I wonder if someone dropped it.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:11.620
But you get hooked, right?

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:13.950
Yeah, it makes me want to smell it.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:15.120
Ah...!

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:16.250
This is it!

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:17.790
What?

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:19.170
Ah...

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:23.090
I'll advance the story
and get to the final episode!

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:24.960
What the heck is he saying?

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:27.670
Yeah. That scent is...

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:30.340
Excuse me! One of you
dropped your handkerchief!

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:33.260
Also, if you like, can we go out
for tea or something some... time?

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.890
Hm?

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:37.390
Oh, that's my handkerchief.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:42.020
You went out of the way and ran
to give it back to me? Thanks.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.570
Go out for tea?
What a wonderful invitation.

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:48.820
I'll... think... about... it.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.780
Wow... You sound so sexy, Capellini-<i>chan</i>.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:52.990
Usahara-<i>kun </i>is aggressive, huh?

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:57.410
With the desperation, he's cuter than
I thought. He might be my type.

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:00.250
What? No way! He's your type?!

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:03.750
Does it look like you can get
to the final episode, Usahara?

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:13.010
Dismissed.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.720
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:16.890
Ugh...

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:20.440
Utano-<i>chan</i>. Life is long. Cheer up.

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:24.230
Yeah... It's only just begun, right?

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.860
Ah!

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:32.110
Uramichi-<i>kun</i>! How about
making full use of CG

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:36.950
and shooting a Hollywood movie,
<i>God of Shiso vs. Bonjour Man</i>?

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:40.330
You can't make a Hollywood
movie just like that!

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.170
Please wake up!

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:44.380
Ahh! Uramichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:17:44.380 --> 00:17:47.000
Uramichi-<i>kun</i>!

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:51.680
Ah...

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:54.470
Hm?

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:58.600
Ah! Uramichi Oniisan!

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:00.770
Good timing!

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:05.810
The thing is, there's something I want
to say to you, Uramichi Oniisan.

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:08.650
What? Wh-What is it?

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:24.170
On second thought, never mind.

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:26.080
Goodbye.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.290
What?

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.250
Kikaku-<i>san</i>...

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:34.260
Why is he saying stuff that strangely
draws my attention, today of all days?

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:36.930
Uramichi Oniisan!

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:44.190
It feels like a final-episode-esque event
may happen today, but it's not...

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:47.560
I feel like they're all duds
and it's kind of annoying.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.520
But you did blow yourself up.

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:51.280
Please stop.

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:53.780
Well, it's hard to notice it, but it means

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:57.990
that everyday life with
no changes makes you feel happy.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:18:59.620
I guess you're right.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.370
Just got married

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:06.290
Well, if I got married, I might retire
from being a singer Oneesan.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:09.790
So, this might mean that I should
focus on my job for today.

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:13.380
I don't want you to retire, Utano Oneesan!

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:16.340
I won't for a while.
Don't make me say that.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:19.720
Hey, you're listening to others,
Iketeru-<i>kun</i>. That's rare.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:27.100
Somehow, this feels the most
like the final episode.

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:29.110
Everyone!

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:31.780
The shoot will start soon!

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:34.990
Okay!

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:42.410
"Together with Maman"

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.790
<i>Together with Maman</i>!

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:47.960
Hello, kids! I'm Uramichi Oniisan!
How are you?!

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:50.840
Hello!

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:50.840
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:19:58.220 --> 00:20:01.550
All right! It's time for
<i>Together with Maman</i>!

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:56.020
Today's shoot is a wrap.
Thank you for your hard work.

00:22:56.020 --> 00:22:57.730
Bye-bye!

00:22:57.730 --> 00:22:59.360
Bye-bye!

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:07.820
Man, I'm exhausted.

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:11.120
Oh, yeah! Let's go out for drinks
with everyone together for a change!

00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:15.500
Oh, sounds good! For some reason,
I want to drink and have fun today.

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:19.340
He won't be home since he's attending
the wedding afterparty anyway.

00:23:19.340 --> 00:23:21.460
You shouldn't drown your sorrows.

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:23.840
What did you say? I wasn't listening.

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:25.720
You're coming, too, right, Uramichi-<i>san</i>?!

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:26.680
No, I'm--

00:23:26.680 --> 00:23:28.350
Okay, you're coming!

00:23:28.350 --> 00:23:32.770
Now that it's decided,
let's get changed already.

00:23:32.770 --> 00:23:38.060
Any adult would be two-faced
or even three-faced.

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:40.440
Ah! Would you like
to go get dinner together?

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:42.610
We were just talking about it.

00:23:42.610 --> 00:23:45.280
Was it okay to force Uramichi-<i>san</i>
to come like that?

00:23:45.280 --> 00:23:49.370
I did it on impulse, but now
I'm afraid to turn around.

00:23:49.370 --> 00:23:53.250
You kids pretend that you
didn't see anything, okay?
